# Source is checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Windows runners default to `core.autocrlf=true`, so `.rs` files arrived with
# CRLF and three tests that read their own source with `include_str!` looked
# for "\n    }\n" and did not find it. They failed only on Windows, and only
# after the tests that read source were added — the checkout, not the code,
# was the difference. Nothing in the repository is committed with CRLF, so
# this changes no content; it fixes what the working tree looks like.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The two that Windows genuinely wants CRLF for.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
*.a binary
